Postgres. Expand/contract pattern: add columns + backfill now, drop `full_name` later in separate migration once app reads new columns. Every statement guarded → re-run safe.

## Migration 1: expand + backfill

```sql
-- 001_split_full_name.sql
-- Idempotent. Run OUTSIDE a wrapping transaction (batch loop COMMITs).

-- 1. Add columns (no-op if present)
ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS first_name text;
ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS last_name  text;

-- 2. Split helper: first token -> first_name, remainder -> last_name
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION split_full_name(p_full text,
                                           OUT first_name text,
                                           OUT last_name  text)
LANGUAGE sql IMMUTABLE AS $$
  WITH n AS (
    SELECT btrim(regexp_replace(coalesce(p_full, ''), '\s+', ' ', 'g')) AS v
  )
  SELECT NULLIF(split_part(v, ' ', 1), ''),
         NULLIF(regexp_replace(v, '^\S+\s*', ''), '')
  FROM n;
$$;

-- 3. Keep new columns in sync while old code still writes full_name
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION users_sync_name_parts()
RETURNS trigger LANGUAGE plpgsql AS $$
BEGIN
  IF TG_OP = 'INSERT'
     OR NEW.full_name IS DISTINCT FROM OLD.full_name THEN
    -- only derive if caller didn't set parts explicitly
    IF NEW.first_name IS NULL AND NEW.last_name IS NULL
       OR (TG_OP = 'UPDATE'
           AND NEW.first_name IS NOT DISTINCT FROM OLD.first_name
           AND NEW.last_name  IS NOT DISTINCT FROM OLD.last_name) THEN
      SELECT s.first_name, s.last_name
        INTO NEW.first_name, NEW.last_name
        FROM split_full_name(NEW.full_name) s;
    END IF;
  END IF;
  RETURN NEW;
END;
$$;

DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS trg_users_sync_name_parts ON users;
CREATE TRIGGER trg_users_sync_name_parts
  BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE ON users
  FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION users_sync_name_parts();

-- 4. Batched backfill. Only touches unconverted rows -> re-run resumes.
DO $$
DECLARE
  batch_size constant int := 5000;
  n int;
BEGIN
  LOOP
    WITH todo AS (
      SELECT id
      FROM users
      WHERE first_name IS NULL
        AND last_name  IS NULL
        AND full_name IS NOT NULL
        AND btrim(full_name) <> ''      -- blank names skipped, else infinite loop
      ORDER BY id
      LIMIT batch_size
      FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
    )
    UPDATE users u
       SET first_name = s.first_name,
           last_name  = s.last_name
      FROM todo, LATERAL split_full_name(u.full_name) s
     WHERE u.id = todo.id;

    GET DIAGNOSTICS n = ROW_COUNT;
    EXIT WHEN n = 0;
    COMMIT;                -- short txns, small lock windows (PG11+)
    PERFORM pg_sleep(0.05); -- ease replication lag
  END LOOP;
END;
$$;

-- 5. Index for lookups (non-blocking; IF NOT EXISTS = re-runnable)
CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF NOT EXISTS idx_users_last_first
  ON users (last_name, first_name);
```

## Migration 2: contract (later, after app deploy reads/writes new cols)

```sql
-- 002_drop_full_name.sql
DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS trg_users_sync_name_parts ON users;
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS users_sync_name_parts();

-- Guard: refuse if backfill incomplete
DO $$
BEGIN
  IF EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.columns
     WHERE table_name = 'users' AND column_name = 'full_name'
  ) AND EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM users
     WHERE first_name IS NULL AND btrim(coalesce(full_name, '')) <> ''
  ) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Unbackfilled rows remain; rerun 001 first';
  END IF;
END;
$$;

ALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS full_name;
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS split_full_name(text);
```

## Rollback for 001

```sql
DROP INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF EXISTS idx_users_last_first;
DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS trg_users_sync_name_parts ON users;
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS users_sync_name_parts();
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS split_full_name(text);
ALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS first_name;
ALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS last_name;
```

## Notes

- **Why safe re-run:** `IF NOT EXISTS`/`OR REPLACE`/`DROP ... IF EXISTS` on DDL; backfill `WHERE first_name IS NULL AND last_name IS NULL` → already-done rows skipped, crash mid-way resumes.
- **Transaction wrapping:** `COMMIT` inside `DO` and `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY` both fail inside transaction block. Flyway/Rails/Alembic etc. wrap by default → disable per-migration (e.g. Rails `disable_ddl_transaction!`, Flyway `executeInTransaction=false`) or split step 5 into own file.
- **Name splitting lossy.** "Mary Ann Smith" → `Mary` / `Ann Smith`; "van der Berg", mononyms, CJK family-name-first all imperfect. Mononym → `last_name` NULL. Don't make `last_name NOT NULL`. Keep `full_name` until 002 so original data recoverable; consider snapshot (`CREATE TABLE users_full_name_bak AS SELECT id, full_name FROM users`) before 002 — drop is irreversible.
- **Blank `full_name`** rows left NULL/NULL deliberately.
- Requires `users.id` PK; Postgres 11+ (`EXECUTE FUNCTION`, txn control in `DO`).
